+## Examples
+
+Each folder under `examples/` is a complete program. Pick one with
+`EXAMPLE`; each gets its own binary under `build/bin/`.
+
+### Showcase
+
+`examples/showcase`. A menu and five demos, each one a `Scene`, each
+built to make one part of the framework obvious.
+
+```
+make EXAMPLE=showcase run
+```
+
+| Demo | What it shows |
+|---|---|
+| Easing playground | every `TransitionFunction` on its own lane; click to retarget them all mid-flight |
+| Particle sandbox | hold left mouse to paint, right click for a `Frame` of `Slider`s that tunes the emitter live; additive blending and bloom |
+| Shake lab | impulses and the sustained floor, a `Gauge` and a live trauma graph, and a HUD you can switch between `get_ui_view()` and the steady default view |
+| Name forge | `Markov` on English, German and callsign lists, typed into a grid of `TextBox`es; names already in the list are drawn dim, so the order slider is easy to read |
+| Shader windows | draggable `Frame` windows, each running its own fragment shader: plasma, a rippling pool, a CRT with three channels, rising fire, and an oscilloscope tracing a chiptune synth or your microphone. Only the window under the cursor gets input |
+
+The shaders are plain GLSL 1.10, so they run on macOS's legacy OpenGL
+too, and each quantises to a four-colour ramp with an ordered dither to
+stay in the pixel-art style. The oscilloscope only makes sound while its
+window is open, and has a mute button.
+
+Number keys open a demo from the menu and escape returns to it. The
+font is Pixel Operator (CC0), drawn at 16px and 32px where it is crisp.
+
